    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"Hurricane Mitch devastated Central America during the months of October- November of 1998. From 1998 to 2001 the US Geological Survey has been involved along with other federal agencies in the reconstruction effort. This CD consists of a compilation of GIS data layers and computer applications focused on hazard prevention and municipal planning. Each dataset includes layers for a base area of one hundred square kilometers around the urban center of each municipality in the Hurricane Mitch project. The size of the study area and number of database layers may vary depending on data availability. Additional information about the Mitch project and data products can be found at the project's web site: http://mitchnts1.cr.usgs.gov.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of this CD collection is to provide support to hazard prevention activities and basic level GIS data for municipalities involved in the Mitch reconstruction efforts and to support the municipalities planning efforts.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
